Because there is no relative velocity between the point of contact and the ground, no work is done by the friction force, so the energy is conserved.

The only role of rolling is to impose the no-slip condition $dot(x) = a dot(theta)$; on a horizontal surface this makes $(dif E)/(dif t) = dot(x) (-f) + dot(theta) (a f) = 0$ for the friction force $f$.
